            "url": "https://languagelog.ldc.upenn.edu/nll/?p=68456"
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Wikipedia, the meme can be pronounced **\"dohzh\"** (/do\u028a\u0292/), **\"dohj\"** (/do\u028ad\u0292/), or **\"dohg\"** (/do\u028a\u0261/).",
        "type": "text"
      },
      {
        "citations": null,
        "text": "\n\nHere are the main camps:\n\n### 1. \ud83c\udfc6 \"Dohzh\" or \"Dohj\" \u2014 The Most Common / \"Official\"\n",
        "type": "text"
      },
      {
        "citations": [
          {
            "cited_text": "The correct pronunciation of Dogecoin is \u201cdohj coin\u201d, which would be written as \u02c8d\u0259\u028a\u0292k\u0254\u026an using the International Phonetic Alphabet (IPA). You can hea...",
            "encrypted_index": "EpEBCioIEBgCIiRkMmJjZWZjOS0wNDQwLTQxYWUtOTM0Mi1hNDFhNjdkYWIzZWQSDIhLRQ7OtfniahV7pxoMcYjKwZXYtKf6eX4bIjCeyf+dRsr/0m1SSyBCynCPxDt55XAIYRO6o/7fKl+GztS0xIC2BT62cDYCdwMO5fUqFYrKk/Vo4VvrGoTel7u1Z7OWigNc8BgE",
            "title": "How to Pronounce Dogecoin? Here's the Right Way to Say It | CoinCodex",
            "type": "web_search_result_location",
            "url": "https://coincodex.com/article/25941/how-to-pronounce-dogecoin/"
          }
        ],
        "text": "The pronunciation **\"dohj\"** (written as /do\u028a\u0292/ in IPA) was confirmed by Dogecoin's co-creator Jackson Palmer, who said the name was inspired by the animated series *Homestar Runner*, where a character spells out D-O-G-E and another character reads it as \"dohj.\"",
        "type": "text"
      },
      {
        "citations": null,
        "text": "\n\n### 2. \"Dohg\" \u2014 Like \"Vogue\" or \"Rogue\"\n",
        "type": "text"
      },
      {
        "citations": [
          {
            "cited_text": "If you\u2019re a hard-G GIF pronouncer, there\u2019s also the alternate form of the same basic structure above, which is \u201cDoh-g\u201d with a long O, hard G and silen...",
            "encrypted_index": "Eo8BCioIEBgCIiRkMmJjZWZjOS0wNDQwLTQxYWUtOTM0Mi1hNDFhNjdkYWIzZWQSDPkwNtwoXuBUQdKAFRoM6BsUGeOedZFSaVGFIjDUzkLuFSIu3/RVrjtzGkfY/dQyCi3vf+7N8xcyE02ook7aaT9ehjFZYLhlw9wgHvgqE5pGK79fiqi6qT52q4MGmVf5Vn4YBA==",
            "title": "How To Pronounce the Doge Meme | The Mary Sue",
            "type": "web_search_result_location",
            "url": "https://www.themarysue.com/much-pronounce/"
          }
        ],
        "text": "Some people pronounce it **\"dohg\"** with a long O, hard G, and silent E \u2014 reasoning that the original word \"dog\" has a hard G, so the E only modifies the vowel, not the consonant \u2014 sort of like how \"slop\" becomes \"slope\" and \"mop\" becomes \"mope.\"",
        "type": "text"
      },
      {
        "citations": null,
        "text": "\n\n### 3. \"Doh-geh\" \u2014 Like \"Doggy\" but fancier\n",
        "type": "text"
